# UI and feedback

- Keep the existing Potta screens and components; extend them instead of introducing a new design system.
- Brand: green `#0B5D1E` / `#237804` (`primary` / `green-700`), lime accent `#A3E46B`, page background `var(--main-bg)`, field fill `var(--field-bg)` / `bg-field`, radius `var(--radius)` (0.25rem). Font is Inter; headings use `font-medium`.
- **Inputs / selects / textareas** on the page canvas and inside white sheets use light grey (`bg-field` via `FIELD_*` / `SHEET_FIELD_*` in `src/lib/field-styles.ts`). Never leave form controls as pure white on white.
- **Selects:** use shadcn `@/components/shadcn/select` for form and filter selects. Keep react-select wrappers only for async typeahead against large lists.
- **List chrome:** search/filters and action buttons share one row via `ListToolbar` (`src/app/(routes)/_shared/states.tsx`) — search left, actions right on `md+`.
- **Sheets / slideovers:** open from the **right** (default `side="right"`). Do not slide create forms in from the left.
- **Page titles:** navbar already shows the page name. Do not add in-page `PageHeader` title/description that duplicates it; keep actions in `ListToolbar` or an actions-only row.
- **Location switcher:** no bordered “Location context” card — compact, borderless trigger.
- **Document / invoice branding:** seller block (logo, name, address, phone, email, registration, tax ID) comes from Auth org profile via `useOrganizationProfile` — never hardcode “Instanvi” or personal emails.
- **Loading:** tables and layoutful panels use Skeleton (`TableSkeleton` / shadcn `Skeleton`) only. Spinners (`PottaLoader`) are for auth/boot, not list bodies.
- Feedback uses Sonner only: `import { toast } from 'sonner'` -> `toast.success`, `toast.error`, `toast.info`, `toast.loading`. Do not use `react-hot-toast` (removed) and do not mount extra `<Toaster />`; `AppProviders` mounts one.
- Destructive actions (delete, void, deactivate, sign out) ask for confirmation in a modal. Never use `window.confirm` or `window.alert`.
- Every list/detail view handles loading, empty and error states.
- Amounts are XAF by default; format with `Intl.NumberFormat` and keep currency from the record when present.
